{"abstract":"In this article, we discuss how and why virtual items known as “skins” travel beyond games and into wider online ecosystems where they become tokens in gambling games. We argue that betting with skins purchased on the Steam platform contributes to the wider platform economy. We do this on the basis of a comparative analysis of Counter-Strike: Global Offensive and Fortnite: Battle Royale as well as the two platforms on which these games exist. First, we discuss the notion of platform economies in relation to the two cases in question and how this positions the consumer as “prosumer” and “micro-entrepreneur.” Second, we introduce our analytical framework related to game economies and skins as commodities and currencies. On the basis of this, we compare the ways skins are acquired in the two games and the degree to which they extend exist beyond the game. We argue that Epic retains a “skin-monopoly,” within the game, whereas Steam features a free “skin market” that transgresses the platform and turns the “prosumer” into a “micro-entrepreneur” and the “modder” into a “speculator.”","author_count":2,"contributors":["Thorhauge, Anne Mette","Nielsen, Rune K.L."],"cuid":["S02-090.32-038355"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Gambling","Market structure","Platform economy","Skins","Steam","Video games","application programing interfaces","skin betting"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"epic steam and the role of skin betting in game platform economies","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1469540521993929","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-090.32-038355","identifier":[{"id":"85102432289","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a3d7ce13-9294-4bd5-9f55-c092e5407311","ku-9f8356c8-dbb8-4845-a0df-41ea490c0223"],"keyword":["Steam","application programing interfaces","gambling","market structure","platform economy","skin-betting","skins","video games"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C6D2F4B037ABA848591BD621E5CB9346"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/291127324/nielsen1469540521993929.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86567057/nielsen1469540521993929.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1469540521993929","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Mette","key":"thorhaugepau","last":"Thorhauge","locid":"db0f4b07-a80b-426a-b445-d0d1e239c178","name":"Thorhauge, Anne Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-5100-5587","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Kristian Lundedal","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"80784458-06f6-4eff-b0c8-df982ffa9835","name":"Nielsen, Rune Kristian Lundedal","orcid":"0000-0002-7209-9041","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1469540521993929","issn":["14695405","17412900"],"issn_org":["14695405"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Consumer Culture","pages":"52","publisher":"Sage Publishing","status":"p","title":"Journal of Consumer Culture","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85102432289"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a3d7ce13-9294-4bd5-9f55-c092e5407311","ku-9f8356c8-dbb8-4845-a0df-41ea490c0223"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Epic, Steam, and the role of skin-betting in game (platform) economies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.32-038355","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we investigate the phenomenon colloquially known as “loot boxes”. Loot boxes became a hot topic towards the end of 2017 when several legislative bodies proposed that they were essentially gambling mechanisms and should therefore be legislated as such. We argue that the term “loot box” and the phenomena it covers are not sufficiently precise for academic use, and instead introduce the notion of “random reward mechanisms” (RRMs). We offer a categorization of RRMs, which distinguishes between RRMs that are either “isolated” from real-world economies or “embedded” in them. This distinction will be useful in discussions about loot boxes in general, but specifically when it comes to the question of whether or not they represent instances of gambling. We argue that all classes of RRMs have gambling-like features, and may be problematic in different ways, but that only one class can be considered to be genuine gambling.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Nielsen, Rune Kristian Lundedal","Grabarczyk, Pawel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677296"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Addiction","Classification","Gambling","In game purchases","Internet gaming disorder","Loot boxes","Microtransactions","Taxonomy","disorder gaming","loot crates","random reward mechanisms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"are loot boxes gambling random reward mechanisms in video games","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84838627/Nielsen_Grabarczyk_2019_._Are_Loot_Boxes_Gambling_Random_reward_mechanisms_in_video_games.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677296","ids":["itu-01077f79-d860-4c26-aacc-28635fadd2db"],"keyword":["addiction","classification","disorder gaming","gambling","in-game purchases","internet gaming disorder","loot boxes","loot crates","microtransactions","random reward mechanisms","taxonomy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6865E7412D32D461DFA6270DA1032240"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84838627/Nielsen_Grabarczyk_2019_._Are_Loot_Boxes_Gambling_Random_reward_mechanisms_in_video_games.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Kristian Lundedal","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"80784458-06f6-4eff-b0c8-df982ffa9835","name":"Nielsen, Rune Kristian Lundedal","orcid":"0000-0002-7209-9041","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pawel","key":"grabarczykpau","last":"Grabarczyk","locid":"42147e05-f94c-471d-a889-c57a01e4bdd0","name":"Grabarczyk, Pawel","orcid":"0000-0002-1268-7474","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["23289422"],"journal":"Transactions of the Digital Games Research Association","pages":"171-207","paperid":"6","status":"p","title":"Transactions of the Digital Games Research Association","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-01077f79-d860-4c26-aacc-28635fadd2db"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Are Loot Boxes Gambling? : Random Reward Mechanisms in Video Games","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677296","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This panel presents a range of contemporary approaches to studying the ongoing convergence between video games, digital gambling, and other new monetization methods. In today's gaming environment, familiar economic capital mixes with gaming capital based on in-game social exchanges and performance, representing a central part of the contemporary ludo mix. With visible and impactful contemporary controversies, and growing legal and regulatory interest, this is a vital moment to consider the evolving roles of gambling in digital games. Given interest in this area from many disciplinary fields and scholars, this panel is designed to rapidly highlight a number of approaches to tackling these emerging questions, especially valuable in such a new and not-yet-formalised area of game studies. It should lay a foundation for the future study, and will bring together and generate conversations between diverse scholars - both in the panel, and attending the panel - with interests in this area.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Thorhauge, Anne Mette","Nielsen, Rune Kristian Lundedal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-455754"],"event":{"end":"2019-08-10","place":"Kyoto, jp","start":"2019-08-06","title":"Digital Games Research Association Conference 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of skinbetting in game platform economies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-455754","ids":["ku-685c23d0-5720-4754-a41a-0c7cd74a85a7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2F1A109109B6491213A870404940AD26"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Mette","key":"thorhaugepau","last":"Thorhauge","locid":"db0f4b07-a80b-426a-b445-d0d1e239c178","name":"Thorhauge, Anne Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-5100-5587","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rune Kristian Lundedal","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Rune Kristian Lundedal","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-685c23d0-5720-4754-a41a-0c7cd74a85a7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The role of skinbetting in game (platform) economies","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-455754","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Esports is the fastest growing sports industry globally, and esports research is becoming more prevalent. However, there is a lack of research on what 21st century skills esports players develop. This study examines the experiences of nine young CS:GO players and their coach enrolled in an esports program at a sports college in the greater Copenhagen area. Through observation and group interviews we try to identify the pedagogical goals of the coach and how these are understood and experienced by the players. Based on Gee’s notion of affinity space and Dialogical Self Theory, we explore how the players position themselves in relation to their esports activities as well as their perception of what it takes to be a competent player. The preliminary findings show that both the players and their coach emphasize healthy culture (‘sund spilkultur’) as a key aspect of the esports activities. Thus, players believe that being able to communicate well and in a respectful tone is a core competency on par with technical skills and understanding of the game. In summary, players report that their experience of better communication skills is an ongoing concern both inside and outside of the game. In addition, the players describe how their ‘people skills’ transfer to friends, family and school work as a result of esports training.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Rune Kristian Lundedal","Hanghøj, Thorkild"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-058161"],"event":{"acronym":"ECGBL","end":"2019-10-04","place":"Odense, dk","start":"2019-10-03","title":"13th European Conference on Games-Based Learning 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["21st Century Skills","Communication","Counter Strike","Game based learning","affinity space","eSport"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"esport skills are people skills","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/311943311/2019_ECGBL_Esports_skills_are_people_skills.doc","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-058161","identifier":[{"id":"85075290554","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1bb968e0-9d2a-4ad4-b03e-5477f7ba7a53"],"keyword":["21st century skills","Counter-Strike","Game-based Learning","affinity space","communication","esport"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-272895D1F6C1A00CB6D9CFCB58384FB9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/311943311/2019_ECGBL_Esports_skills_are_people_skills.doc","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Kommunikation - IT og Læringsdesign","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Culture and Learning, ILD-LAB – Research lab for IT and Learning Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, The Center for Applied Game Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Kristian Lundedal","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Rune Kristian Lundedal","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thorkild","key":"hanghøjpau","last":"Hanghøj","locid":"f14a3800-5086-4fa8-880e-ac0725c8756d","name":"Hanghøj, Thorkild","orcid":"0000-0001-8053-8377","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars","key":"elbaekpedh","last":"Elbaek","name":"Elbaek, Lars","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Gunver","key":"majgaardpedh","last":"Majgaard","name":"Majgaard, Gunver","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrea","key":"valentepedh","last":"Valente","name":"Valente, Andrea","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Saifuddin","key":"khalidpedh","last":"Khalid","name":"Khalid, Saifuddin","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.34190/gbl.19.041","eisbn":["9781912764372"],"isbn":["9781912764389"],"issn":["20490992"],"pages":"535-542","place":"Reading","publisher":"Academic Conferences International (ACI)","series":"Proceedings of the European Conference on Games-based Learning","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 13th European Conference on Game-Based Learning"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075290554"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1bb968e0-9d2a-4ad4-b03e-5477f7ba7a53"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"eSport skills are people skills","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-058161","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Esports is the fastest growing sports industry globally, and esports research is becoming more prevalent. However, there is a lack of research on what 21st century skills esports players develop. This study examines the experiences of nine young CS:GO players and their coach enrolled in an esports program at a sports college in the greater Copenhagen area. Through observation and group interviews we try to identify the pedagogical goals of the coach and how these are understood and experienced by the players. Based on Gee’s notion of affinity space and Dialogical Self Theory, we explore how the players position themselves in relation to their esports activities as well as their perception of what it takes to be a competent player. The preliminary findings show that both the players and their coach emphasize healthy culture (‘sund spilkultur’) as a key aspect of the esports activities. Thus, players believe that being able to communicate well and in a respectful tone is a core competency on par with technical skills and understanding of the game. In summary, players report that their experience of better communication skills is an ongoing concern both inside and outside of the game. In addition, the players describe how their ‘people skills’ transfer to friends, family and school work as a result of esports training.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Rune Kristian Lundedal","Hanghøj, Thorkild"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381477"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["21st Century Skills","Communication","Counter Strike","Esports","affinity space"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"esports skills are people skills","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-g